  "interpretation": {
    "0x1f": "The fixed parser maps byte 0x1f to KeyCode::Char('7') with CONTROL (c - 0x1c + b'4'), not to a printable character.",
    "0x1f_not_ctrl_slash": "0x1f is the legacy control-byte path; Ctrl-/ is handled by Codex compatibility logic when the terminal reports Ctrl-7, while enhanced CSI-u can report explicit codepoint/modifier.",
    "pty_driver": "The repository PTYDriver responds only to cursor-position query ESC[6n with ESC[1;1R. It has no keyboard-enhancement response handler; therefore the fixed parser cannot establish that this PTY enabled keyboard enhancement."
  },
